## 1. Pre-use notice (control FIN-CPR-005)

*Shown clearly and conspicuously before the technology is used.*

> **We use automated decision-making technology in this process.** [Name of institution] uses an automated tool to help evaluate [describe the decision, e.g. "applications for credit cards"]. The tool [describe its role, e.g. "estimates the likelihood that a loan will be repaid; a credit officer reviews applications that fall below our approval threshold"].
>
> To learn more about how this technology is used, [instructions: link, phone number, or address].
>
> If a decision is made against you, you have rights, including to receive an explanation, to ask us to correct inaccurate personal information used, and to request human review. [Summarize the rights as finally required.]

## 2. Post-adverse-outcome disclosure (control FIN-CPR-006)

*Sent within 30 days of an adverse outcome that the technology materially influenced.*

> **About our decision on your [application].** On [date], we [describe the decision]. An automated tool played the following role in this decision: [plain-language description of the tool's role].
>
> The main factors were: [principal reasons; for credit decisions, use the same reasons as your adverse-action notice].
>
> You can [request more information / ask us to correct inaccurate personal information we used / ask for a person to review the decision] by [simple-to-follow instructions]. [Add any other content required by law or rule.]

